{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-60138","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89745","text":"stackdocs — specification"}]},{"id":"blk-60139","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89746","text":"What this system is, what it must do, what it must never do, and how to tell a correct implementation from a wrong one. Derived from the code at "},{"id":"spn-89747","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-89748","text":" in the ProjectAmp2 monorepo."}]},{"id":"blk-60140","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89749","text":"1. Purpose"}]},{"id":"blk-60141","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89750","text":"stackdocs produces a single self-contained HTML file ("},{"id":"spn-89751","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/index.html"},{"id":"spn-89752","text":") and a machine-readable sidecar ("},{"id":"spn-89753","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/atlas.json"},{"id":"spn-89754","text":") that together mirror every documentation markdown file across the [&] monorepo as a navigable site. The site's routes are the source paths; an agent or a human can map between the two without a lookup table."}]},{"id":"blk-60142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89755","text":"The build also produces one BendScript document per source file ("},{"id":"spn-89756","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/bend/*.bend.json"},{"id":"spn-89757","text":"), each validated and content-addressed."}]},{"id":"blk-60143","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89758","text":"2. Invariants"}]},{"id":"blk-60144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89759","text":"These properties must hold on every successful build. A build that violates any of them must fail, not degrade."}]},{"id":"blk-60145","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89760","text":"2.1 Route-source identity"}]},{"id":"blk-60146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89761","text":"For every page, "},{"id":"spn-89762","marks":["code"],"text":"route === source path"},{"id":"spn-89763","text":". The build must not move, rename, or re-root any file. A reader seeing route "},{"id":"spn-89764","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-89765","text":" must be able to open that exact path on disk."}]},{"id":"blk-60147","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89766","text":"2.2 BendScript validity"}]},{"id":"blk-60148","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89767","text":"Every page must be a valid BendScript document per the "},{"id":"spn-89768","marks":["code"],"text":"@bendscript/core"},{"id":"spn-89769","text":" schema. A document that cannot be validated degrades to a raw code-block view but is still validated in that form — it is never omitted."}]},{"id":"blk-60149","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89770","text":"2.3 Content-address fixpoint"}]},{"id":"blk-60150","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89771","text":"Every page is content-addressed (CIDv1). The round-trip "},{"id":"spn-89772","marks":["code"],"text":"parse(serialize(parse(doc)))"},{"id":"spn-89773","text":" must produce the same CID. This is checked across the entire corpus; a single violation fails the "},{"id":"spn-89774","marks":["code"],"text":"fixpointAll"},{"id":"spn-89775","text":" flag in the build report."}]},{"id":"blk-60151","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89776","text":"2.4 Build provenance"}]},{"id":"blk-60152","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89777","text":"Every build embeds a git commit hash as both a "},{"id":"spn-89778","marks":["code"],"text":"<meta name=\"build-commit\">"},{"id":"spn-89779","text":" tag and a field in the model JSON. The commit is derived from the latest non-"},{"id":"spn-89780","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89781","text":" commit ("},{"id":"spn-89782","marks":["code"],"text":"git log -1 --format=%H -- . \":(exclude)dist\""},{"id":"spn-89783","text":"), not from HEAD. This is the \"two-commit chain\" strategy: source changes are committed first (the "},{"id":"spn-89784","marks":["italic"],"text":"source commit"},{"id":"spn-89785","text":"), then "},{"id":"spn-89786","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89787","text":" is rebuilt and committed on top (the "},{"id":"spn-89788","marks":["italic"],"text":"artifact commit"},{"id":"spn-89789","text":"). The provenance always points to the source commit, breaking the self-referential cycle where committing "},{"id":"spn-89790","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89791","text":" would change HEAD, which would change the embedded hash, which would require another commit."}]},{"id":"blk-60153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89792","text":"If no source commit can be resolved to a 40-hex-char SHA, the build fails. The build date is derived from the source commit's timestamp, not the wall clock, so that repeated builds of the same source commit produce byte-identical output regardless of when the artifact commit is made."}]},{"id":"blk-60154","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89793","text":"2.5 Derived facts, not literals"}]},{"id":"blk-60155","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89794","text":"Canonical numbers (versions, law counts, trial counts) are read at build time from the file that owns them — "},{"id":"spn-89795","marks":["code"],"text":"package.json"},{"id":"spn-89796","text":" for npm versions, "},{"id":"spn-89797","marks":["code"],"text":"mix.exs"},{"id":"spn-89798","text":" for Elixir versions, the conformance harness source for law counts. A missing or unreadable source is a hard build failure. No fallback to a stale literal exists. The mechanism lives in "},{"id":"spn-89799","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89800","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-60156","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89801","text":"2.6 Cross-doc link integrity"}]},{"id":"blk-60157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89802","text":"Relative "},{"id":"spn-89803","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-89804","text":" links within the corpus that resolve to a known route become internal navigation edges. Unresolvable links degrade gracefully (they render as-is) but do not fail the build. The curated build ("},{"id":"spn-89805","marks":["code"],"text":"build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89806","text":") is stricter: a broken internal edge is a hard failure."}]},{"id":"blk-60158","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89807","text":"3. The dark factory"}]},{"id":"blk-60159","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89808","text":"The build derives a four-phase status model called the \"dark factory\" from "},{"id":"spn-89809","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_COMPLETION.md"},{"id":"spn-89810","text":". The four phases, in fixed order, are:"}]},{"id":"blk-60160","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89811","marks":["bold"],"text":"perceive"},{"id":"spn-89812","text":" — sourced from §4 step 1"}]}],"id":"blk-60161","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60164","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89813","marks":["bold"],"text":"decide"},{"id":"spn-89814","text":" — an explicit GAP (no step in §4 owns a decision-phase evidence rung)"}]}],"id":"blk-60163","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89815","marks":["bold"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-89816","text":" — sourced from §4 step 1"}]}],"id":"blk-60165","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60168","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89817","marks":["bold"],"text":"measure"},{"id":"spn-89818","text":" — sourced from §4 step 7"}]}],"id":"blk-60167","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89819","text":"Each sourced phase carries an evidence-ladder rung parsed from the owning table row. The valid rungs are: "},{"id":"spn-89820","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-89821","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89822","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-89823","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89824","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-89825","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89826","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-89827","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89828","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-89829","text":". A phase with no owning source is recorded as a named GAP with an explanatory string, not fabricated."}]},{"id":"blk-60170","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89830","text":"3.1 Dark-factory constraints"}]},{"id":"blk-60171","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89831","text":"The phase count must be exactly four, in the order above."}]}],"id":"blk-60172","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60175","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89832","text":"A GAP must not carry a rung or a source field."}]}],"id":"blk-60174","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89833","text":"The presentation layer ("},{"id":"spn-89834","marks":["code"],"text":"home.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89835","text":") must not contain any hard-coded evidence-rung literals ("},{"id":"spn-89836","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-89837","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89838","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-89839","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89840","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-89841","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89842","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-89843","text":"). The word "},{"id":"spn-89844","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-89845","text":" is allowed because it collides with the ship-status vocabulary; the unambiguous rung literals are the test boundary."}]}],"id":"blk-60176","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89846","text":"These constraints are enforced by "},{"id":"spn-89847","marks":["code"],"text":"test-dark-factory.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89848","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-89849","marks":["code"],"text":"npm test"},{"id":"spn-89850","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-60178","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60180","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89851","text":"4. The verification gate"}]},{"id":"blk-60181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89852","marks":["code"],"text":"verify-deployed.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89853","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-89854","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run verify:deployed"},{"id":"spn-89855","text":") is the gate for the docs reporting claim to reach "},{"id":"spn-89856","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-89857","text":". It:"}]},{"id":"blk-60182","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89858","text":"Fetches the production site at "},{"id":"spn-89859","marks":["code"],"text":"https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com"},{"id":"spn-89860","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-60183","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89861","text":"Extracts the embedded commit hash and model JSON."}]}],"id":"blk-60185","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89862","text":"Verifies internal consistency (meta tag commit === model commit)."}]}],"id":"blk-60187","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89863","text":"Checks that the local source commit (latest non-"},{"id":"spn-89864","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89865","text":" commit) matches the production commit. Under the two-commit chain, this is the commit that produced the build, not HEAD."}]}],"id":"blk-60189","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89866","text":"Rebuilds locally from the same source."}]}],"id":"blk-60191","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89867","text":"Compares the dark-factory model field-by-field: phase order, rungs, sources, GAP status and text."}]}],"id":"blk-60193","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89868","text":"Checks that the production HTML contains visible references to "},{"id":"spn-89869","marks":["code"],"text":"darkFactory"},{"id":"spn-89870","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89871","marks":["code"],"text":"GAP"},{"id":"spn-89872","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-89873","marks":["code"],"text":"source"},{"id":"spn-89874","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-60195","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89875","text":"Fails if any divergence is found, including commit parity."}]}],"id":"blk-60197","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89876","text":"The script does not deploy. It only asserts that what is deployed matches what the source produces."}]},{"id":"blk-60200","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89877","text":"5. Deployment"}]},{"id":"blk-60201","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89878","text":"Deployment is a manual "},{"id":"spn-89879","marks":["code"],"text":"sync-docs.sh"},{"id":"spn-89880","text":" invocation that:"}]},{"id":"blk-60202","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60204","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89881","text":"Rebuilds the atlas from the live monorepo."}]}],"id":"blk-60203","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60206","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89882","text":"Clones the deploy repo ("},{"id":"spn-89883","marks":["code"],"text":"c-u-l8er/docs"},{"id":"spn-89884","text":") into a temp directory."}]}],"id":"blk-60205","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60208","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89885","text":"Mirrors "},{"id":"spn-89886","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89887","text":" into the clone."}]}],"id":"blk-60207","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89888","text":"Commits and pushes only if something changed."}]}],"id":"blk-60209","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89889","text":"Cloudflare Pages serves the deploy repo's "},{"id":"spn-89890","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89891","text":" verbatim with no build step. The deploy repo is not this repo — it is a separate git repository that receives pre-built artifacts."}]},{"id":"blk-60212","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89892","text":"6. Two build modes"}]},{"id":"blk-60213","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89893","text":"The codebase has two build pipelines:"}]},{"id":"blk-60214","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89894","marks":["bold"],"text":"`build-atlas.mjs`"},{"id":"spn-89895","text":" (primary, "},{"id":"spn-89896","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run build"},{"id":"spn-89897","text":") — filesystem-mirror mode. Scans the entire monorepo, ingests every "},{"id":"spn-89898","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-89899","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89900","marks":["code"],"text":"prompts/"},{"id":"spn-89901","text":" markdown file. Produces the homepage theme system (Runefort bands), the dark-factory model, and the atlas sidecar. This is what ships."}]}],"id":"blk-60215","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60218","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89902","marks":["bold"],"text":"`build.mjs`"},{"id":"spn-89903","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-89904","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run build:curated"},{"id":"spn-89905","text":") — curated mode. A hand-authored 21-page proof-of-concept defined entirely in "},{"id":"spn-89906","marks":["code"],"text":"content.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89907","text":". Stricter link checking (broken internal edge = build failure). Supports transclusion ("},{"id":"spn-89908","marks":["code"],"text":"{{key}}"},{"id":"spn-89909","text":"). Does not scan the filesystem. Does not produce "},{"id":"spn-89910","marks":["code"],"text":"atlas.json"},{"id":"spn-89911","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-60217","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89912","text":"The reason for keeping both is not recorded in the code. The curated build appears to be the earlier prototype; the atlas build superseded it for production use."}]},{"id":"blk-60220","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89913","text":"7. Must-never-do"}]},{"id":"blk-60221","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89914","text":"Must never move, rename, or reorganize source files. The mirror property is load-bearing."}]}],"id":"blk-60222","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60225","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89915","text":"Must never hard-code a fact (version, count) that has a canonical source file. The derivation in "},{"id":"spn-89916","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89917","text":" is the only path."}]}],"id":"blk-60224","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89918","text":"Must never hard-code evidence-rung literals in the presentation layer."}]}],"id":"blk-60226","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60229","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89919","text":"Must never produce a deployment without a resolvable commit hash."}]}],"id":"blk-60228","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89920","text":"Must never silently succeed when a canonical source is missing or unreadable."}]}],"id":"blk-60230","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89921","text":"Must never fabricate a dark-factory rung or source for a phase that has no owning step."}]}],"id":"blk-60232","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60234","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89922","text":"8. Dependencies"}]},{"id":"blk-60235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89923","text":"Two runtime dependencies, both from the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-60236","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89924","marks":["code"],"text":"@bendscript/core"},{"id":"spn-89925","text":" 0.1.0-alpha.0 — validation, content-addressing, serialization, parsing."}]}],"id":"blk-60237","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89926","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-89927","text":" 0.10.0 — imported by "},{"id":"spn-89928","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89929","text":" path traversal (law counting), not used as a runtime governance kernel in this codebase."}]}],"id":"blk-60239","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60241","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89930","text":"No other runtime dependencies. The build runs on Node.js with only built-in modules beyond these two."}]},{"id":"blk-60242","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89931","text":"9. Open questions"}]},{"id":"blk-60243","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89932","text":"These are decisions the code makes whose reasons are not recorded:"}]},{"id":"blk-60244","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89933","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why keep the curated build?"},{"id":"spn-89934","text":" "},{"id":"spn-89935","marks":["code"],"text":"build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89936","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89937","marks":["code"],"text":"content.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89938","text":" are a complete second pipeline with hand-authored content. The atlas build superseded it for production. Whether the curated build is still exercised, depended on, or slated for removal is not stated."}]}],"id":"blk-60245","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89939","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why does `box-and-box` appear in `package.json`?"},{"id":"spn-89940","text":" It is listed as a dependency but "},{"id":"spn-89941","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89942","text":" reads from the monorepo path "},{"id":"spn-89943","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/"},{"id":"spn-89944","text":", not from "},{"id":"spn-89945","marks":["code"],"text":"node_modules"},{"id":"spn-89946","text":". The installed package may be unused. The reason for its inclusion is not recorded."}]}],"id":"blk-60247","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89947","marks":["bold"],"text":"Fallback-vs-failure asymmetry."},{"id":"spn-89948","text":" The atlas build treats an unparseable document as a graceful fallback (raw code block); the curated build treats a broken internal edge as a hard failure. Both are defensible but the difference in failure philosophy is not explained."}]}],"id":"blk-60249","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60251","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89949","text":"10. What is already written down elsewhere"}]},{"id":"blk-60252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89950","text":"The referenced ADR documents ("},{"id":"spn-89951","marks":["code"],"text":"ADR-0004"},{"id":"spn-89952","text":" through "},{"id":"spn-89953","marks":["code"],"text":"ADR-0008"},{"id":"spn-89954","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89955","marks":["code"],"text":"SUPERVISOR.md"},{"id":"spn-89956","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89957","marks":["code"],"text":"workbench spec"},{"id":"spn-89958","text":") are about WebHost.Systems and the workbench, not about this codebase. They share vocabulary (deployment immutability, provenance, telemetry) but do not describe stackdocs. The "},{"id":"spn-89959","marks":["code"],"text":"README.md"},{"id":"spn-89960","text":" in this directory is the closest thing to a prior spec; this document supersedes it for normative purposes."}]},{"id":"blk-60253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89961","text":"No design document for this codebase existed before this file."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierap4s6s6yglqlthuhmqsgcghjtwu5haiifartmhgwkj74lna34eawq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}